+
+### Bug fix: Steam depot uploads were sweeping in every old build sitting in release/, not just the newest one (patch 0395)
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Bug Fix
+
+- Fixed Steam uploads including every old build ever packaged instead of just the newest one
+```
+
+Direct report + steamcmd log evidence: a Steam upload sat scanning content
+for several minutes before even starting to upload, well past what a
+~400MB app should take. The pasted log confirmed it: "Scanning content"
+found **11.3GB** before uploading anything.
+
+**Root cause (`generateSteamBuildScripts()` in `tools/devtool/server.mjs`).**
+The depot's `FileMapping` used `"LocalPath" "*"` with `"recursive" "1"` --
+ContentRoot's entire contents, not the newest build specifically. Nothing
+in this tool or electron-builder itself clears out `release/` between
+Package runs, so it had accumulated "heaps" of old installers (the
+reporter's own words) from prior sessions, and every single one got
+scooped into the same VDF as the one build actually meant to ship.
+
+**Fix.** `FileMapping`'s `LocalPath`/`DepotPath` now name the exact file
+`findLatestReleaseFile()` already identifies as the newest installer --
+the same lookup Generate already used to build the `desc` field, just not
+previously used to narrow what gets mapped. `recursive` is dropped
+entirely (a single named file has nothing to recurse into), and the three
+`FileExclusion` entries (`win-unpacked*`, `*.blockmap`, `latest.yml`) are
+gone too -- they existed only to carve exceptions out of a whole-folder
+scan that no longer happens; naming one exact file already excludes
+everything else in `release/` by construction.
+
+**Not done, out of scope for this pass:** old builds already sitting in
+`release/` from before this patch aren't cleaned up automatically --
+worth clearing that folder by hand once (keep the current newest build,
+delete the rest). Nothing in this codebase currently automates that
+cleanup; worth a follow-up if it keeps growing.
+
+**Verified:** re-read `findLatestReleaseFile()`'s return shape
+(`{ full, name, mtimeMs }`) to confirm `latest.name` is the bare filename
+`generateSteamBuildScripts()` needs (not the full path, which
+`ContentRoot` already supplies) -- matches how `latest.name` was already
+being used one line below in `desc`. No live steamcmd run in this
+environment to confirm the resulting VDF actually uploads a sane content
+size -- worth watching the "Scanning content" line on the next real
+upload to confirm it now reports roughly the actual installer size
+instead of the whole folder.
